# Staged Design Workflow (D0–D7)

**Purpose:** Force **design-before-code** and **dependency tracing** before implementation. The agent must not begin coding immediately after a basic plan.

**Principle:** Spend more time designing, tracing dependencies, and searching for bugs **before and after** implementation. Practical depth scales by feature class (§8).

**Legacy mapping:** D0≈CP0 baseline; D1–D2≈CP0–CP1 discovery; D3≈CP4 pre-DB; D4≈CP4 architecture; D5≈CP1 UI; D6≈CP2 test plan; D7≈threat model; implementation follows D7; post-impl → [adversarial-bug-hunt](adversarial-bug-hunt.mdoc).

---

## 1. Hard gate

**No application source implementation** until mandatory design stages for the session tier (§8) are complete and recorded in session artifacts.

Allowed before D-gates complete:

- Read-only discovery (grep, graph, file read, runtime inspection)
- Session artifact writes under `.cache/feature-delivery/<sessionId>/`
- Markdoc/doc proposals on protected paths (doc-first covenant)

---

## 2. D0 — Repository baseline

**When:** Session start, before D1.

**Record:**

| Field | Source |
| ----- | ------ |
| Branch | `git branch --show-current` |
| HEAD | `git rev-parse HEAD` |
| Upstream | `git rev-parse --abbrev-ref @{upstream}` or null |
| Working tree | `git status --short` |
| Unrelated WIP | Paths outside `scopePaths` |
| Package structure | Root `package.json`, `pnpm-workspace.yaml`, AGENTS.md |
| Available scripts | Relevant `pnpm run` / filter scripts for touched surfaces |
| Runtime services | API/Web/Portal/Marketing dev commands; ports from AGENTS.md |
| Database | `DATABASE_URL` set; `STORAGE_DRIVER`; Postgres vs memory |
| Browser | Playwright configs; smoke scripts for target app |
| Test infrastructure | Existing unit/integration/e2e specs for scope |

**Artifact:** `.cache/feature-delivery/<sessionId>/baseline.json`

**Ledger:** `gate_id=bootstrap.baseline`, checkpoint `D0`

---

## 3. D1 — Product and user journey discovery

**When:** Before coding; expands requirement inventory.

**Identify:**

- Target actors (member, operator, admin, viewer, system)
- User goals and operator/admin goals
- System-triggered behavior (outbox, cron, webhooks)
- Entry points (routes, BFF, commands, events)
- Expected outputs and permission boundaries
- Success, failure, empty, loading, denied states
- Audit requirements and **explicit exclusions**

**Requirement matrix columns:**

| Column | Description |
| ------ | ----------- |
| `requirementId` | Stable ID (e.g. `REQ-001`) |
| `actor` | Who triggers or receives |
| `expectedBehavior` | Observable outcome |
| `currentImplementation` | `complete` \| `partial` \| `missing` \| `unknown` |
| `evidence` | Spec, route, producer, or `none` |
| `risk` | `low` \| `medium` \| `high` \| `critical` |
| `status` | Inventory status per [completion-rules](completion-rules.mdoc) |

**Artifact:** `.cache/feature-delivery/<sessionId>/requirements-matrix.json`

Also maintain `requirement-queue.json` for execution ordering.

---

## 4. D2 — Existing-system and consumer analysis

**When:** Before boundary or contract decisions.

**Trace through:**

- Routes, BFFs, API contracts, services, repositories
- Database models, migrations, RLS policies
- Outbox/events, consumers, UI components
- Existing tests, workspace manifests, adjacent modules

**Search for:**

- Duplicate implementations, parallel tables, duplicate event names
- Inconsistent IDs, incompatible payloads
- Existing and **future** consumers (≥2 for shared concepts)
- Hidden feature gates, workspace-specific behavior (Denali/Urban/starter)

**Artifact:** `.cache/feature-delivery/<sessionId>/consumer-and-boundary-map.json`

**Rule:** Shared platform candidates require ≥2 real consumers before choosing boundary — [architecture-classifier](architecture-classifier.mdoc).

---

## 5. D3 — Data and contract design

**When:** Before database, HTTP contract, outbox, or shared payload changes.

**Define:**

- Canonical field names; request/response shapes
- Null/default behavior; state transitions
- Idempotency keys; deduplication rules; row versioning
- Tenant scope; RLS strategy; migration strategy
- Backward compatibility; event envelope and payload
- Retry and failure behavior

**Edge cases to design tests for:**

`null`, `empty`, `zero`, `false`, `duplicate`, `stale`, `missing`, `malformed`, `out-of-order`, `partial`, `unauthorized`, `cross-tenant`

**Artifact:** `.cache/feature-delivery/<sessionId>/data-contract-map.json`

**Skip when:** Tier A UI-only with no API/contract change (document skip in baseline).

---

## 6. D4 — Architecture and security review

**When:** Before implementation when any trigger applies:

- Shared platform code
- Database schema / Prisma
- `workspace-sdk` / `platform-core`
- Event/outbox/notification/inbox
- Identity, permission, tenant routing
- Financial data

**Review:**

- Module vs platform boundary; future consumers
- Denali/Urban/starter isolation; tenant isolation; authorization
- RLS; sensitive data exposure; internal vs member projection
- Migration safety; idempotency; durability; retry; failure recovery

**Invoke architecture-reviewer** when triggers apply — record verdict before code.

**Artifact:** `.cache/feature-delivery/<sessionId>/architecture-review.json` (or `arch-review.json`)

---

## 7. D5 — UI/UX and information architecture

**When:** Before any user-visible implementation.

**Actions:**

- Inspect existing placement; reuse existing tab/page when possible
- Member vs operator IA; Denali tokens and primitives
- UI UX Pro Max when available — [FDA-INTEGRATION](../../.cursor/skills/ui-ux-pro-max/FDA-INTEGRATION.md)
- Desktop/mobile; FA RTL / EN LTR
- Loading, empty, error, denied, long content, accessibility
- Success/error feedback; before/after screenshot plan

**Artifact:** `.cache/feature-delivery/<sessionId>/ui-ux-decision.json` (24 sections per [research-and-design-gate](research-and-design-gate.mdoc) §3.3)

**Hard gate:** No UI implementation before D5 complete for visible features.

---

## 8. D6 — Test design and test-realness review

**When:** Before implementation (design tests first).

**Design coverage for:**

- Happy and negative paths; boundary values
- Permissions; tenant isolation; stale state
- Duplicate actions; retries; concurrency
- Refresh/reload; mobile; RTL/LTR; accessibility
- Empty, error, loading states

**Classify existing tests:**

| Class | Meaning |
| ----- | ------- |
| `real-e2e` | Real browser/API/Postgres on critical path |
| `partially-mocked` | Some real boundaries; document mocks |
| `api-only` | HTTP without UI or persistence proof |
| `fixture-only` | Direct DB insert as sole proof |
| `static-dom` | Render-only; no interaction |
| `skipped` | Skipped assertions or suite |
| `flaky` | Intermittent without root-cause fix |
| `unverified` | Not run this session or insufficient |

**Rule:** A test cannot prove a feature if it bypasses the critical behavior.

**Artifact:** `.cache/feature-delivery/<sessionId>/test-plan-and-realness.json`

---

## 9. D7 — Threat and failure-mode analysis

**When:** Before coding; **mandatory** for financial, identity, permission, notification, tenant features.

**Identify behavior when:**

- Request repeated; network fails; DB write succeeds but response fails
- Event delivered twice; data stale; tenant or permission changes
- After reload; after process restart; partial configuration
- Invalid input; concurrent operators

**Artifact:** `.cache/feature-delivery/<sessionId>/failure-mode-analysis.json`

---

## 10. Workflow tiers (practical depth)

| Tier | When | Mandatory stages | Notes |
| ---- | ---- | ---------------- | ----- |
| **A — UI-only reduced** | Copy/layout/styling; no API/DB/contract change | D0, D1 (light), D5, D6 (UI-focused) | Skip D3; D4/D7 light unless permission copy |
| **B — API/DB full** | API routes, repositories, migrations, BFF | D0–D7 | Full data/security workflow |
| **C — Platform deepest** | Shared platform, finance, permission, notification, tenant, outbox | D0–D7 full depth + all [adversarial passes](adversarial-bug-hunt.mdoc) | architecture-reviewer at D4; Postgres RLS proof |

Record `workflowTier` in `baseline.json` and `SESSION.lock`.

---

## 11. Implementation entry

After mandatory D-stages for tier:

1. Produce CP2-style implementation plan (sequencing, scopePaths, rollback)
2. First **vertical slice** — smallest end-to-end path
3. Follow [implementation cycle](adversarial-bug-hunt.mdoc) §2 for each finding
4. Run [adversarial bug-hunt passes](adversarial-bug-hunt.mdoc) B1–B8 after slice and before final verdict

**Forbidden:** Symptom fix in UI when root cause is API, contract, persistence, or authorization.

---

## 12. Session artifact checklist

| Artifact | Stage | Required when |
| -------- | ----- | ------------- |
| `baseline.json` | D0 | Always |
| `requirements-matrix.json` | D1 | Always |
| `consumer-and-boundary-map.json` | D2 | Tier B/C; recommended A |
| `data-contract-map.json` | D3 | Tier B/C with contract/DB |
| `architecture-review.json` | D4 | Tier B/C triggers; always C |
| `ui-ux-decision.json` | D5 | User-visible features |
| `test-plan-and-realness.json` | D6 | Always |
| `failure-mode-analysis.json` | D7 | Tier B/C; mandatory C + regulated domains |

---

_Staged design workflow — FDA-001 v1.4.0._
